{"path":".agents/skills/triage/AGENT-BRIEF.md","ref":"2c167c094b21500cfcbf4733064d83f6a69dc4f7","side":"old","lines":[{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":1,"text":"# Writing Agent Briefs"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":2,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":3,"text":"An agent brief is a structured comment posted on a GitHub issue or PR when it moves to `ready-for-agent`. It is the authoritative specification that an AFK agent will work from. The original body and discussion are context — the agent brief is the contract."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":4,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":5,"text":"The brief states **what the agent should do**, which stretches to both surfaces: for an issue, that's building the change from nothing; for a PR, it's what's left to do *to the existing diff* — finish it, close gaps, address review points. Same principles either way; the PR example below shows the difference."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":6,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":7,"text":"## Principles"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":8,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":9,"text":"### Durability over precision"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":10,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":11,"text":"The issue may sit in `ready-for-agent` for days or weeks. The codebase will change in the meantime. Write the brief so it stays useful even as files are renamed, moved, or refactored."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":12,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":13,"text":"- **Do** describe interfaces, types, and behavioral contracts"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":14,"text":"- **Do** name specific types, function signatures, or config shapes that the agent should look for or modify"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":15,"text":"- **Don't** reference file paths — they go stale"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":16,"text":"- **Don't** reference line numbers"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":17,"text":"- **Don't** assume the current implementation structure will remain the same"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":18,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":19,"text":"### Behavioral, not procedural"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":20,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":21,"text":"Describe **what** the system should do, not **how** to implement it. The agent will explore the codebase fresh and make its own implementation decisions."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":22,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":23,"text":"- **Good:** \"The `SkillConfig` type should accept an optional `schedule` field of type `CronExpression`\""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":24,"text":"- **Bad:** \"Open src/types/skill.ts and add a schedule field on line 42\""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":25,"text":"- **Good:** \"When a user runs `/triage` with no arguments, they should see a summary of issues needing attention\""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":26,"text":"- **Bad:** \"Add a switch statement in the main handler function\""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":27,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":28,"text":"### Complete acceptance criteria"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":29,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":30,"text":"The agent needs to know when it's done. Every agent brief must have concrete, testable acceptance criteria. Each criterion should be independently verifiable."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":31,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":32,"text":"- **Good:** \"Running `gh issue list --label needs-triage` returns issues that have been through initial classification\""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":33,"text":"- **Bad:** \"Triage should work correctly\""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":34,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":35,"text":"### Explicit scope boundaries"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":36,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":37,"text":"State what is out of scope. This prevents the agent from gold-plating or making assumptions about adjacent features."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":38,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":39,"text":"## Template"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":40,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":41,"text":"```markdown"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":42,"text":"## Agent Brief"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":43,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":44,"text":"**Category:** bug / enhancement"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":45,"text":"**Summary:** one-line description of what needs to happen"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":46,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":47,"text":"**Current behavior:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":48,"text":"Describe what happens now. For bugs, this is the broken behavior."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":49,"text":"For enhancements, this is the status quo the feature builds on."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":50,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":51,"text":"**Desired behavior:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":52,"text":"Describe what should happen after the agent's work is complete."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":53,"text":"Be specific about edge cases and error conditions."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":54,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":55,"text":"**Key interfaces:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":56,"text":"- `TypeName` — what needs to change and why"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":57,"text":"- `functionName()` return type — what it currently returns vs what it should return"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":58,"text":"- Config shape — any new configuration options needed"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":59,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":60,"text":"**Acceptance criteria:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":61,"text":"- [ ] Specific, testable criterion 1"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":62,"text":"- [ ] Specific, testable criterion 2"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":63,"text":"- [ ] Specific, testable criterion 3"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":64,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":65,"text":"**Out of scope:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":66,"text":"- Thing that should NOT be changed or addressed in this issue"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":67,"text":"- Adjacent feature that might seem related but is separate"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":68,"text":"```"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":69,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":70,"text":"## Examples"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":71,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":72,"text":"### Good agent brief (bug)"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":73,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":74,"text":"```markdown"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":75,"text":"## Agent Brief"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":76,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":77,"text":"**Category:** bug"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":78,"text":"**Summary:** Skill description truncation drops mid-word, producing broken output"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":79,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":80,"text":"**Current behavior:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":81,"text":"When a skill description exceeds 1024 characters, it is truncated at exactly"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":82,"text":"1024 characters regardless of word boundaries. This produces descriptions"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":83,"text":"that end mid-word (e.g. \"Use when the user wants to confi\")."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":84,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":85,"text":"**Desired behavior:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":86,"text":"Truncation should break at the last word boundary before 1024 characters"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":87,"text":"and append \"...\" to indicate truncation."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":88,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":89,"text":"**Key interfaces:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":90,"text":"- The `SkillMetadata` type's `description` field — no type change needed,"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":91,"text":"  but the validation/processing logic that populates it needs to respect"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":92,"text":"  word boundaries"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":93,"text":"- Any function that reads SKILL.md frontmatter and extracts the description"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":94,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":95,"text":"**Acceptance criteria:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":96,"text":"- [ ] Descriptions under 1024 chars are unchanged"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":97,"text":"- [ ] Descriptions over 1024 chars are truncated at the last word boundary"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":98,"text":"      before 1024 chars"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":99,"text":"- [ ] Truncated descriptions end with \"...\""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":100,"text":"- [ ] The total length including \"...\" does not exceed 1024 chars"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":101,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":102,"text":"**Out of scope:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":103,"text":"- Changing the 1024 char limit itself"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":104,"text":"- Multi-line description support"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":105,"text":"```"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":106,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":107,"text":"### Good agent brief (enhancement)"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":108,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":109,"text":"```markdown"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":110,"text":"## Agent Brief"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":111,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":112,"text":"**Category:** enhancement"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":113,"text":"**Summary:** Add `.out-of-scope/` directory support for tracking rejected feature requests"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":114,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":115,"text":"**Current behavior:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":116,"text":"When a feature request is rejected, the issue is closed with a `wontfix` label"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":117,"text":"and a comment. There is no persistent record of the decision or reasoning."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":118,"text":"Future similar requests require the maintainer to recall or search for the"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":119,"text":"prior discussion."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":120,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":121,"text":"**Desired behavior:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":122,"text":"Rejected feature requests should be documented in `.out-of-scope/<concept>.md`"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":123,"text":"files that capture the decision, reasoning, and links to all issues that"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":124,"text":"requested the feature. When triaging new issues, these files should be"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":125,"text":"checked for matches."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":126,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":127,"text":"**Key interfaces:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":128,"text":"- Markdown file format in `.out-of-scope/` — each file should have a"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":129,"text":"  `# Concept Name` heading, a `**Decision:**` line, a `**Reason:**` line,"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":130,"text":"  and a `**Prior requests:**` list with issue links"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":131,"text":"- The triage workflow should read all `.out-of-scope/*.md` files early"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":132,"text":"  and match incoming issues against them by concept similarity"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":133,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":134,"text":"**Acceptance criteria:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":135,"text":"- [ ] Closing a feature as wontfix creates/updates a file in `.out-of-scope/`"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":136,"text":"- [ ] The file includes the decision, reasoning, and link to the closed issue"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":137,"text":"- [ ] If a matching `.out-of-scope/` file already exists, the new issue is"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":138,"text":"      appended to its \"Prior requests\" list rather than creating a duplicate"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":139,"text":"- [ ] During triage, existing `.out-of-scope/` files are checked and surfaced"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":140,"text":"      when a new issue matches a prior rejection"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":141,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":142,"text":"**Out of scope:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":143,"text":"- Automated matching (human confirms the match)"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":144,"text":"- Reopening previously rejected features"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":145,"text":"- Bug reports (only enhancement rejections go to `.out-of-scope/`)"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":146,"text":"```"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":147,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":148,"text":"### Good agent brief (PR)"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":149,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":150,"text":"For a PR, \"Current behavior\" describes the state of the diff, and the brief asks the agent to finish or fix it rather than build from scratch."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":151,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":152,"text":"```markdown"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":153,"text":"## Agent Brief"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":154,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":155,"text":"**Category:** enhancement"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":156,"text":"**Summary:** Finish the contributor's `--json` output flag for `triage list`"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":157,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":158,"text":"**Current behavior:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":159,"text":"The PR adds a `--json` flag that serializes the issue list to JSON. The happy"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":160,"text":"path works and the diff matches the project's command structure. Two gaps"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":161,"text":"remain: errors are still printed as human text (not JSON), and the new flag has"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":162,"text":"no test coverage."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":163,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":164,"text":"**Desired behavior:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":165,"text":"With `--json`, all output — including errors — is well-formed JSON on stdout,"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":166,"text":"and the command's exit codes are unchanged. The existing human-readable output"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":167,"text":"is untouched when the flag is absent."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":168,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":169,"text":"**Key interfaces:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":170,"text":"- The command's error path should emit `{ \"error\": string }` under `--json`"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":171,"text":"  instead of the plain-text error"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":172,"text":"- Reuse the existing serializer the PR already added; don't introduce a second"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":173,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":174,"text":"**Acceptance criteria:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":175,"text":"- [ ] `triage list --json` emits valid JSON for both success and error cases"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":176,"text":"- [ ] Exit codes match the non-JSON command"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":177,"text":"- [ ] A test covers the `--json` success output and one error case"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":178,"text":"- [ ] Default (non-JSON) output is byte-for-byte unchanged"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":179,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":180,"text":"**Out of scope:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":181,"text":"- Adding `--json` to any other command"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":182,"text":"- Changing the JSON shape of the success payload the PR already defined"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":183,"text":"```"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":184,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":185,"text":"### Bad agent brief"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":186,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":187,"text":"```markdown"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":188,"text":"## Agent Brief"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":189,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":190,"text":"**Summary:** Fix the triage bug"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":191,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":192,"text":"**What to do:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":193,"text":"The triage thing is broken. Look at the main file and fix it."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":194,"text":"The function around line 150 has the issue."},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":195,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":196,"text":"**Files to change:**"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":197,"text":"- src/triage/handler.ts (line 150)"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":198,"text":"- src/types.ts (line 42)"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":199,"text":"```"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":200,"text":""},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":201,"text":"This is bad because:"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":202,"text":"- No category"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":203,"text":"- Vague description (\"the triage thing is broken\")"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":204,"text":"- References file paths and line numbers that will go stale"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":205,"text":"- No acceptance criteria"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":206,"text":"- No scope boundaries"},{"sha":"2a2d7910207a4ef9a7d29c77f8ba2e904a638be0","author":"matemolnar8","timestamp":1783544569,"line":207,"text":"- No description of current vs desired behavior"}]}
